# Increment's intervening "if" (CR 702.191a, 603.4): checked again as the ability resolves, against the Colony's power and toughness then. Cuboid Colony (1/1) is on the
# battlefield and Bot1 casts Capital Guard (2 mana, more than 1): increment triggers. With the trigger on the stack Bot1 casts Giant Growth ({G}, 1 mana, not more than 1/1, so no
# trigger of its own) on the Colony; it resolves first and makes the Colony 4/4 - and when the increment ability resolves 2 mana is no longer more than its power or
# its toughness, so it gets no counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Cuboid Colony
Giant Growth
Capital Guard
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cuboid Colony.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Capital Guard.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Growth.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Cuboid Colony)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cuboid Colony.Power = 4
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cuboid Colony.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Cuboid Colony.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Capital Guard.Power = 2
